id: E14724
trigger_tool: make|conan
phase: packaging
error_signature: make install.*up to date|expected installed artifact missing after make install
severity: 2
category: make, packaging, build-system
match_keywords: PHONY, install target, same-named file, up to date, missing installed artifact
title: A shipped file named install can suppress a legacy Make install recipe
root_cause: GNU Make treats a target named install as a filesystem target unless it is declared phony. A release archive can contain an ordinary file named install; then make install exits successfully without executing the installation commands, leaving the Conan package empty or incomplete.
affected_scope: Hand-written legacy Makefiles with command targets that collide with ordinary release files; first confirm the target rule and file identity. This does not apply when install is already PHONY or is a directory target with real dependencies.
verification_cmd: Run make install in the target Conan package() phase and assert the installed library and public header both exist.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: mark-command-target-phony
rec_description: Match exactly one install rule in the temporary source copy, add .PHONY for that command target, run make install, then fail closed unless the expected library and header are present in the package folder.
rec_command: Add .PHONY: install before the exact Makefile install rule; rerun make install -j1.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: explicit-recipe-invocation
fallback_description: If the project's Make syntax cannot be changed safely, invoke only the verified install recipe through a bounded project-specific target after proving it has equivalent semantics; do not treat a zero exit code alone as installation evidence.
fallback_command: Inspect the release Makefile and package folder, then use a verified project-specific installation route.
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: make install.*exit 0.*package complete
forbid_1_reason: A Make no-op may return zero because the ordinary same-named file already exists.
forbid_1_consequence: Empty or partial Conan artifact despite green build command.
